## Engineering update: 2026-10-05

The live course page now records source incident #4471 as closed on 5 October. The parser is **FIXED** by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`; [parser ticket #1](https://github.com/michups/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) is therefore completed. The hint is **WON'T FIX** because the booking-v3 form was retired; [hint ticket #2](https://github.com/michups/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) is closed as not planned, not as a completed fix.

Closure does not mean both defects were repaired. The counts below remain the historical export's report membership, and the exceptional timing symptoms are not independently explained by this update. The separate deduplication decision remains a proposal requiring desk approval.

## Evidence and counts

<IncidentReview />

## Parser: month-first interpretation of day-first dates

The shared parser reads month first even for a tenant whose locale writes day first. An April booking entered as `07/04/2026` can become July 4 rather than April 7. This is a parsing contract problem: use the tenant's declared locale or an explicit, unambiguous date representation, and keep date-only values distinct from instants.

App and email reports belong here under the existing rules, as do form reports that do not use the conflicting month-first hint. Browser locale and intake tags do not determine the tenant's configuration. Acceptance checks should cover each supported day-first locale, ambiguous dates, days over twelve, and round trips through the invite.

## Hint: booking-v3 advertises a different date order

The booking-v3 hint prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, while the day-first tenant's form reads dates in the tenant's order. A user follows the hint and types `04/07/2026` for April 7, but the form can read July 4. Fix the displayed hint and its input contract together; changing only the shared parser does not correct misleading instructions.

This issue covers form-channel reports from day-first tenants running booking-v3. Acceptance checks should compare the visible hint, tenant locale, entered value, and saved date. The two tickets should cross-reference each other without merging their counts.

